    "narrative": "Our lineup construction today leans heavily into favorable matchups against vulnerable starters, with **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Taylor Ward** (70.58) emerging as our most potent options. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Sugano, leveraging a 19% boost from the SP skill profile and an elite leadoff spot. **Taylor Ward** remains a must-start due to the park factor and the premium on his leadoff position, despite a slight drag from his dynamic platoon split. While **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) rounds out our elite tier, **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.21) remains an undervalued asset today; his ability to contribute across categories, specifically in the scarcest category of stolen bases, makes his matchup against Abbott a high-leverage opportunity to gain ground in the standings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Drew Gilbert**, who missed the 40-point efficiency floor with a 38.69 score. His platoon disadvantage against Rolison, coupled with a bottom-of-the-order projection, made him the odd man out in favor of prioritizing the lineup stability of **Jung Hoo Lee**, who\u2014despite his own struggles against lefties\u2014occupies a more secure role. We are monitoring the status of **Bryson Stott** closely; he was penalized heavily today by a tough matchup against Harrison and a lower-order assignment, confirming the optimizer\u2019s strict adherence to our 40-point threshold. With both **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Cal Raleigh** currently sidelined on the IL, the depth of our bench is being tested, though we remain optimistic that the high-ceiling output from **Gavin Sheets** and **Tyler Freeman** will help stabilize our production across the board today.",
